::ENG2_U05_L01_Q01::[MLA.ENG2.L.01] Which sentence is a fragment?{
=A. Because many students need a quiet place after school.#Correct. This begins with "because" but does not complete the thought.
~B. Many students need a quiet place after school.#Incorrect. This is a complete sentence.
~C. The library provides a quiet study space.#Incorrect. This is a complete sentence.
~D. Students can finish assignments in the library.#Incorrect. This is a complete sentence.
}

::ENG2_U05_L01_Q02::[MLA.ENG2.L.01] Which revision fixes the run-on sentence: "The library closes early, students work in loud hallways"?{
~A. The library closes early, students work in loud hallways.#Incorrect. This keeps the comma splice.
=B. When the library closes early, students work in loud hallways.#Correct. This correctly connects the dependent clause to the complete thought.
~C. The library closes early students work in loud hallways.#Incorrect. This is still a run-on.
~D. The library closes, early students, work in loud hallways.#Incorrect. This punctuation is confusing and incorrect.
}

::ENG2_U05_L01_Q03::[MLA.ENG2.V.01] Which word is most precise in this sentence: "The library gives students a quiet place to complete assignments"?{
~A. thing#Incorrect. This is vague.
~B. stuff#Incorrect. This is vague and informal.
=C. provides#Correct. "Provides" is precise and academic.
~D. nice#Incorrect. This is general and imprecise.
}

::ENG2_U05_L01_Q04::[MLA.ENG2.W.04] Which revision best fits a formal request to school leaders?{
~A. Keep the library open because it is awesome.#Incorrect. This is too informal.
~B. The library should be open, yeah.#Incorrect. This is informal and vague.
~C. I just want it open.#Incorrect. This is too personal and unsupported.
=D. Extending library hours would give students a supervised place to study after school.#Correct. This is formal, specific, and audience-aware.
}

::ENG2_U05_L01_Q05::[MLA.ENG2.L.01] Which sentence uses a comma correctly after an introductory clause?{
=A. When the library closes early, students often work in loud hallways.#Correct. The comma follows the introductory dependent clause.
~B. When, the library closes early students often work in loud hallways.#Incorrect. The comma is placed incorrectly.
~C. When the library closes early students, often work in loud hallways.#Incorrect. The comma separates the subject from the verb phrase.
~D. Students often, work in loud hallways when the library closes early.#Incorrect. The comma unnecessarily separates the subject and verb.
}

::ENG2_U05_L01_Q06::[MLA.ENG2.L.01] Which sentence is complete?{
~A. Because students ride late buses.#Incorrect. This is a fragment.
=B. Students who ride late buses need a safe place to study.#Correct. This has a subject, verb, and complete thought.
~C. When assignments are due.#Incorrect. This is a fragment.
~D. A quiet place after school.#Incorrect. This lacks a verb and complete thought.
}

::ENG2_U05_L01_Q07::[MLA.ENG2.L.01] Which sentence contains a comma splice?{
~A. Students need a quiet place because hallways are loud.#Incorrect. This sentence is correctly joined.
~B. The library provides tables, computers, and supervision.#Incorrect. These commas correctly separate list items.
=C. Students need a quiet place, the library can provide it.#Correct. Two complete thoughts are joined with only a comma.
~D. When the library opens, students can study.#Incorrect. This comma is correct after an introductory clause.
}

::ENG2_U05_L01_Q08::[MLA.ENG2.W.04] Which revision is most audience-aware for school leaders?{
~A. The library is cool and should stay open.#Incorrect. This is informal.
~B. Everyone wants the library open.#Incorrect. This overgeneralizes.
~C. Keep it open because I said so.#Incorrect. This is not appropriate for the audience.
=D. Extended library hours would support students who need a quiet place to complete assignments after school.#Correct. This explains the benefit clearly and formally.
}

::ENG2_U05_L01_Q09::[MLA.ENG2.R.10] Original: "Students often complete assignments in loud hallways when the library closes early." Which paraphrase is accurate?{
=A. When the library is not available after school, students may have to work in noisy hallways.#Correct. This keeps the meaning in new words.
~B. Students never complete assignments.#Incorrect. This contradicts the original.
~C. The library is always loud.#Incorrect. The original says hallways are loud.
~D. Students do not need study spaces.#Incorrect. This changes the meaning.
}

::ENG2_U05_L01_Q10::[MLA.ENG2.L.01] Which revision fixes the fragment: "After the last bus arrives."{
~A. After the last bus arrives and.#Incorrect. This is still incomplete.
=B. After the last bus arrives, students can leave campus safely.#Correct. This completes the thought.
~C. After the last bus.#Incorrect. This is still a fragment.
~D. Arrives after last bus students.#Incorrect. This is unclear.
}

::ENG2_U05_L01_Q11::[MLA.ENG2.V.01] Which phrase uses the most precise academic vocabulary?{
~A. a good place#Incorrect. This is vague.
~B. a nice thing#Incorrect. This is vague and informal.
=C. a supervised study space#Correct. This phrase is specific and academic.
~D. a place for stuff#Incorrect. This is informal and unclear.
}

::ENG2_U05_L01_Q12::[MLA.ENG2.L.01] Which sentence is correctly punctuated?{
~A. Students need a quiet place, because hallways are loud.#Incorrect. The comma before "because" is unnecessary here.
~B. Students need a quiet place because, hallways are loud.#Incorrect. The comma is placed incorrectly.
~C. Students need, a quiet place because hallways are loud.#Incorrect. The comma separates the verb from its object.
=D. Students need a quiet place because hallways are loud.#Correct. No comma is needed in this sentence.
}

::ENG2_U05_L01_Q13::[MLA.ENG2.W.04] Which sentence should be revised for a formal audience?{
=A. The library should stay open because it is awesome.#Correct. "Awesome" is too informal for a formal request.
~B. The library provides a quiet study space.#Incorrect. This is formal and clear.
~C. Extended hours would support students who ride late buses.#Incorrect. This is appropriate for the audience.
~D. Students need a supervised place to work after school.#Incorrect. This is appropriate and clear.
}

::ENG2_U05_L01_Q14::[MLA.ENG2.L.01] Which correction best combines these sentences? "The library closes early. Students lose a quiet place to work."{
~A. The library closes early students lose a quiet place to work.#Incorrect. This is a run-on.
=B. When the library closes early, students lose a quiet place to work.#Correct. This shows the relationship clearly.
~C. The library closes early, students lose a quiet place to work.#Incorrect. This is a comma splice.
~D. Because the library closes early.#Incorrect. This is a fragment.
}

::ENG2_U05_L01_Q15::[MLA.ENG2.L.01] Which sentence has a pronoun clarity problem?{
~A. The library closes at four o'clock.#Incorrect. This sentence has no unclear pronoun.
~B. Students need a quiet place to study.#Incorrect. This sentence is clear.
=C. When students asked teachers about the library, they said it should stay open.#Correct. The pronoun "they" could refer to students or teachers.
~D. The library provides computers for research.#Incorrect. This sentence is clear.
}

::ENG2_U05_L01_Q16::[MLA.ENG2.R.10] Which paraphrase best preserves the meaning of "The library provides students with a supervised place to complete assignments"?{
~A. Students are not allowed to complete assignments.#Incorrect. This contradicts the original.
~B. The library has no adults present.#Incorrect. This contradicts supervised.
~C. Assignments are never completed in the library.#Incorrect. This changes the meaning.
=D. The library gives students a monitored space where they can finish schoolwork.#Correct. This keeps the meaning using new wording.
}

::ENG2_U05_L01_Q17::[MLA.ENG2.L.01] Which sentence is a run-on?{
=A. The library has computers students can use them after school.#Correct. Two complete thoughts are joined without punctuation or a connector.
~B. The library has computers that students can use after school.#Incorrect. This is complete and correctly joined.
~C. Students can use library computers after school.#Incorrect. This is a complete sentence.
~D. After school, students can use library computers.#Incorrect. This is correctly punctuated.
}

::ENG2_U05_L01_Q18::[MLA.ENG2.W.04] Which sentence is clearest for an academic paragraph?{
~A. The thing is good for people.#Incorrect. This is vague.
=B. Extended library hours would help students complete assignments in a quiet setting.#Correct. This is specific, clear, and audience-aware.
~C. It is nice and stuff.#Incorrect. This is informal and unclear.
~D. There are some reasons, maybe.#Incorrect. This is vague and uncertain.
}

::ENG2_U05_L01_Q19::[MLA.ENG2.L.01] Which sentence correctly uses a semicolon?{
~A. The library should stay open; because students need a quiet place.#Incorrect. A semicolon should join two complete thoughts, and the second part is dependent.
~B. The library; should stay open because students need a quiet place.#Incorrect. The semicolon splits the subject and verb.
=C. The library should stay open; students need a quiet place after school.#Correct. The semicolon joins two related complete thoughts.
~D. The library should; stay open students need a quiet place.#Incorrect. The semicolon is placed incorrectly.
}

::ENG2_U05_L01_Q20::[MLA.ENG2.V.01] Which revision improves the vague phrase "a lot of kids"?{
~A. tons of kids#Incorrect. This is still informal.
~B. many people and stuff#Incorrect. This is vague.
~C. a bunch of students#Incorrect. This is informal.
=D. many students#Correct. This is clear and appropriate for academic writing.
}

::ENG2_U05_L01_Q21::[MLA.ENG2.L.01] Which sentence best fixes this comma splice: "Students need computers, the library has them"?{
=A. Students need computers, and the library has them.#Correct. The coordinating conjunction correctly joins the two complete thoughts.
~B. Students need computers, the library has them.#Incorrect. This keeps the comma splice.
~C. Students need computers the library has them.#Incorrect. This is a run-on.
~D. Because students need computers.#Incorrect. This is a fragment.
}

::ENG2_U05_L01_Q22::[MLA.ENG2.W.04] Which sentence best explains why conventions matter for audience?{
~A. Conventions are just rules with no purpose.#Incorrect. Conventions help readers understand meaning.
=B. Correct conventions help readers follow ideas without confusion.#Correct. This explains how conventions support communication.
~C. Conventions make every sentence longer.#Incorrect. Conventions do not automatically make sentences longer.
~D. Conventions replace evidence.#Incorrect. Conventions support clarity but do not replace evidence.
}

::ENG2_U05_L01_Q23::[MLA.ENG2.L.01] Which sentence should be revised because it is incomplete?{
~A. The library should remain open after school.#Incorrect. This is complete.
~B. Students often need a quiet place to study.#Incorrect. This is complete.
=C. While students wait for late buses.#Correct. This dependent clause is incomplete by itself.
~D. Extended hours could support student learning.#Incorrect. This is complete.
}

::ENG2_U05_L01_Q24::[MLA.ENG2.R.10] Which paraphrase changes the meaning incorrectly? Original: "Extended library hours would support students who ride late buses."{
~A. Keeping the library open longer would help students waiting for late buses.#Incorrect. This is accurate.
~B. Students who ride late buses would benefit from longer library hours.#Incorrect. This is accurate.
~C. Longer library hours could support students after school.#Incorrect. This keeps the general meaning.
=D. Students who ride late buses do not need the library.#Correct. This contradicts the original meaning.
}

::ENG2_U05_L01_Q25::[MLA.ENG2.L.01] Which revision is the most polished final sentence?{
=A. Because many students need a quiet place after school, the library should remain open until late buses depart.#Correct. This sentence is complete, clear, and correctly punctuated.
~B. Because many students need a quiet place after school.#Incorrect. This is a fragment.
~C. Many students need a quiet place, the library should remain open until late buses depart.#Incorrect. This is a comma splice.
~D. Students quiet place library open buses.#Incorrect. This is unclear.
}
